WEBVTT

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.980
Commander, abnormality in the enemy
quantum portal! It's overloading!

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.150
All vessels, emergency withdrawal!

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:28.460
Impossible!
The Gards-orm blew up the quantum portal?!

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.560
The Oceanus has lost its path back to Earth.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.010
They may as well be
considered captives now.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.610
New enemy formation at 4 o'clock!

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.340
Kobrals and Nautiluses, a total of 14!

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.510
All Zegapain units are
currently engaged in battle!

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:42.780
Barrage, full spread!

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:52.590
<i>If we can't stop the</i>
<i>advance of the deutera zone,</i>

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:55.180
<i>that leaves capturing</i>
<i>Cloud base our only option.</i>

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:21.120
<i>This is the first time an actual</i>
<i>person has operated the Zegapain.</i>

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:26.450
<i>With a human hand with blood flowing</i>
<i>through it grasping the control grip.</i>

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.660
<i>This is the moment</i>
<i>he's waited so long for.</i>

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:43.230
<i>And also...</i>
<i>The moment when Kyo and I must part forever.</i>

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:16.170
No hesitations now, huh, Kyo?

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:17.810
It's a weird feeling.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:20.040
I have two sets
of 16-year-old memories.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:22.750
I'm sorry.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:24.480
You have nothing to apologize for.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.550
No, it's all my fault...

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:28.220
I said no!

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:34.280
You're wrong.
The one who should apologize is me.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:40.660
Really?
Maihama sounds like a lot of fun!

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:45.870
I've had to live through the same stuff
three times since becoming a Cerebrant,

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.670
but each time,
I discover something new.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:50.370
I'd like to go see it myself.

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:53.580
If we manage to realize
Commander Shima's plan,

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:56.580
then Maihama and the
meta-bodies still asleep now...

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:58.950
will all be able
to return to the Earth.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:10.230
You can't become human?

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.420
Yes. Just me.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:13.960
Why not?!

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:17.300
I only consist of quantum data.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.030
So, even if the resurrection
system is perfected...

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.440
No way...

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:28.130
<i>Back then,</i>
<i>I still didn't understand.</i>

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:31.540
<i>About feeling for people,</i>
<i>being thought of by people...</i>

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:34.840
<i>About sharing feelings</i>
<i>with each other.</i>

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:37.380
<i>And then...</i>

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:41.030
<i>Extensive damage to the Altair!</i>

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:43.330
<i>Dry damage to Gunner now at the limit!</i>

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:47.030
<i>Meta-body C.H.I.P. loss rate</i>
<i>entering danger zone.</i>

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:50.730
<i>Wet damage upon transmission recovery</i>
<i>and data restoration now unavoidable.</i>

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:54.770
This is goodbye.

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:56.800
Wait! I'll stay to the very end!

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:01.010
Be strong and live, Shizuno.

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:05.680
Even if they bring me back,
I won't be me any more.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.250
Even so...

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:10.150
I'll come to you! I promise!

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:12.250
Kyo!

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:16.920
KYO!!!

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:25.890
I'm thankful I was able
to have another chance at life.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:28.730
Because now...

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:31.640
I WON'T LET IT BE LOST!

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:40.410
Abyss!

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:01.370
How thoughtful of you!
The Hraesvelg's got a full Q.L. charge!

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:04.140
Don't expect any congratulations.

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:06.630
That's something I'd have done
before I became one with Naga.

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:09.410
There is something I wanted
to ask you about, though.

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:14.290
Wouldn't you agree that the Oceanus
has enough Q.L. left on board...

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:16.280
to make it a pretty good bomb?

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:20.150
Mission phase 4...
Destroy G-Phaetus?!

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:24.860
I've been wondering if that glowing ball
that looks like the Earth below here...

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:26.630
might be some sort of weak point.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.960
What's your opinion, Lemures?

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:35.130
You'll be destroyed, too.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:39.370
We were right.
You heard the man, Kyo!

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:45.670
We're blowin' this place apart
and going back to Earth!

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.600
Be careful, Kyo!

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:03.060
Defeat for the Altair means
losing the Maihama server!

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:04.840
I know that!

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:07.200
Not just that.
You'll lose your life, too.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:08.500
Right!

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.420
Why?

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:30.860
Why did we, the more evolved,
lose to the lightless ones?

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:32.990
Why?

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:45.740
Why were we given eternal life?

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:50.440
You were afraid of losing it.

00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:53.810
That's why you wanted eternity.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.550
You really are...
such a nice person...

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:03.490
Are you Sin's friend?

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:05.230
Yeah.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:08.160
We'll... see each other again... soon...

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.500
I'll come back to life...

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:15.040
Because Sin's life... is eternal...

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.410
Eternity has ended.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:33.080
The last Sin is gone.

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:36.420
Sin...

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:41.290
I'll never forget it. Your name...

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:47.830
You fools.
You fools! You fools!

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:50.540
Who wants eternity?

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:53.030
Please, bring this to an end...

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:55.710
KYO!!!

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:11.200
Is that... Could it be?!

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:13.330
Huge explosion on the lunar surface!

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:15.530
All functions within
G-Phaetus have ceased!

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:16.830
And the Oceanus?

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.640
No response!

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:21.610
Was it destroyed along with G-Phaetus?!

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:25.540
The enemy has lost its command
network and is in chaos!

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:26.510
They're being annihilated!

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:36.520
Kobrals, wiped out!

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:39.160
3 floating gun turrets
have targeted us!

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:40.590
Mop them up with
the vulcan phalanx!

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:46.400
The Gards-orm have been destroyed.

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:50.600
But the chance for mankind's
rebirth has also been lost forever.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:53.570
They're not destroyed!
The Gards-orm are still fine!

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:06.750
What happened?!

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:09.920
Cloud's quantum portal is activated!
It's transmitted something!

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:11.620
I'm into their circuits!
We have video!

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:21.790
Zegapain Altair...

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:38.020
The escape was successful!

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:40.310
<i>Kyo! Yehl! Are you all right?!</i>

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:42.220
Commander Isola!

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:44.380
Transmit Chris and May-yen aboard!

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:46.050
Roger!

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:49.950
Are you okay, May-yen?

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:58.300
The Arctic core server
is running autonomously,

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:00.740
so the deutera zone
is still expanding.

00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:04.410
Total envelopment of the Earth
will occur in 9 hours, 7 minutes.

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:06.010
We have to do this.

00:10:06.010 --> 00:10:07.350
Before <i>he</i> gets here!

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:07.810
Right.

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:23.330
We've got access.
That's as much as I can do from here on.

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:26.790
Sorry, but I need your
help to do what I can't.

00:10:27.130 --> 00:10:30.530
Right.
I've been waiting for this moment.

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:32.830
<i>What are you two planning to do?!</i>

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:35.910
We're invading Cloud's control system...

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:39.770
and launching deutera cores
aimed at the Arctic core server.

00:10:40.210 --> 00:10:41.550
You're what?!

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:43.210
<i>Cool, huh?</i>

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:45.680
<i>We thought up</i>
<i>this mission on our own!</i>

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:50.050
A deutera core will be able to
penetrate the barrier around Sabato.

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:53.820
If we shoot the cores like missiles into it,
we'll destroy the core server!

00:10:54.330 --> 00:10:55.460
<i>It's reckless!</i>

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:57.150
There's no other way!

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:02.290
Quantum weapon detected, closing fast!

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:11.340
I'm going.

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:12.840
Listen...

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:15.470
Don't trade your life to end this war.

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:19.310
I know how you feel.

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.210
I'm sorry.

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:26.780
And also... Thank you.

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:31.820
I was so happy when
you were brought back.

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:38.130
You changed, but I changed, too.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:42.800
I finally awoke from
a nightmare and became human.

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:46.570
Kyo... I loved you.

00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:49.040
And I loved you.

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:50.910
Goodbye.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.610
This isn't goodbye. Promise me!

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:56.750
I'll try hard.

00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:05.560
Shizuno.

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:15.730
Security!

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:24.370
I won't let you interfere, Abyss!

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:33.650
Kyo... Sogoru!

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:43.160
Kyo Sogoru...
Why do you not accept eternity?

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:46.130
Why won't you appreciate eternal life?!

00:12:46.770 --> 00:12:50.940
That's my own business!
Figure it out for yourself, you dumb ass!

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:03.810
What?!

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:09.890
Handle navigation!

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:32.610
If I can just break this barrier,
I'm into the control system...

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:38.150
Why, you!

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:47.520
You're good.
You're no pushover!

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:53.830
What?

00:13:57.210 --> 00:13:59.680
I thought it didn't matter
if I made it back or not.

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:03.450
But... I have to get back!
I <i>want</i> to get back!

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:06.140
Back to Kyo! To where Kyo is!

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:08.680
<i>You will get back!</i>
<i>With the rest of us!</i>

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:15.790
Minato.

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:20.520
Man, is there any limit
on how reckless you two will be?

00:14:20.970 --> 00:14:23.170
Still, it doesn't look like
there's any other choice.

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:25.860
Yeah, right. Except I'm still
not clear on what's going on.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:28.340
Definitely.

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:29.400
Everyone...

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:33.380
Now, while you can!
Take over Cloud's control system!

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:34.880
Shizuno!

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:35.870
Gotcha!

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:52.890
Anything goes, huh?
Fine with me!

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:56.490
In that case, lemme show you
a secret move of my own!

00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:58.230
BANISHMENT MODE!

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:04.800
But just in the left arm!

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:08.730
MAIHAMA SHINING OCEAN PUNCH!!!

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:29.500
Abyss, the place where
our battle ends...

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:31.970
IS RIGHT HERE!!!

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:20.680
I've gotta get going.
Wake up already, Kyo.

00:16:24.590 --> 00:16:26.960
Oh, morning, big brother.

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:28.590
Oh. Good morning.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:33.060
Listen! Dad was saying we should go
somewhere while he's got time off.

00:16:33.060 --> 00:16:36.260
So, why don't you invite <i>her?</i>
That upperclassman you've got a crush on...

00:16:40.840 --> 00:16:45.110
<i>Right. A dream.</i>
<i>This is just a dream.</i>

00:16:45.110 --> 00:16:48.340
<i>If one world is real,</i>
<i>then the other must be a dream.</i>

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:51.340
<i>But, which one?</i>

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:57.890
Minato-sempai!

00:16:58.520 --> 00:17:02.360
At last!
Minato-sempai's bare legs!

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:04.850
Screw the nationals,
we're headed for the world championship!

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:09.690
<i>Thank you for this, Commander Shima.</i>

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:19.540
Summer break's over.
Time for the second semester to begin.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:21.280
Yeah.

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:27.440
Second semester...
It has a fresh ring to it, huh? Why is that?

00:17:27.890 --> 00:17:30.120
Who knows?

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:36.890
Life's funny, isn't it?

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:40.330
Because life has limits,

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:44.770
people love and cherish
everything in this world.

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:48.830
Maybe that's why we love
this moment called "now."

00:17:49.470 --> 00:17:51.530
Is that <i>his</i> influence?

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:54.140
Maybe I'll say something
different tomorrow!

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:56.200
I've got the result!

00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:57.680
Lu-shen!

00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:02.450
We can do it. It's possible with the
improved meta-body resurrection program.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:04.010
Really?!

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:05.720
So, Shizuno, too?

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:06.980
Yeah.

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:12.360
You should sound happier!
One day we can do it!

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:15.070
You'll be a human,
like the rest of us!

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:18.200
I'm sure he did this all for you.

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:23.540
Um... I'm sorry, but I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:28.110
I see. Your memory...

00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:30.740
Sorry.
We were just a little excited.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.150
You both are so funny.

00:18:37.790 --> 00:18:40.090
Something born from nothingness.

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:43.250
And without trying to,
mankind becomes more like God.

00:18:43.860 --> 00:18:46.260
What would Naga think
if he knew about this?

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:49.130
Never mind that,
now I'm worried about what'll happen.

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:52.800
If Shizuno becomes human,
we'll have a love triangle on our hands.

00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:58.340
That won't be bad, either.

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:04.480
Gards-orm remnant forces, withdrawing.

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:06.470
Toga and Meivelle are returning to the ship.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:11.210
After the Zegapains are hangared,
the ship will carry out a supply mission.

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:14.290
Oh, yeah.
Today's our semimonthly trip.

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:19.320
He'll be grumbling again.
"I'm sick of this canned food you dig up for me!"

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:22.730
<i>"I want a decent meal</i>
<i>of white rice," right?</i>

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:27.130
Right, full rudder!
Set course for Japan!

00:19:33.140 --> 00:19:34.970
"A man's life is but 50 years."

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:39.480
"It is but a dream,
an illusion in the great order of things."

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:47.520
Strictly speaking, you could say that
one could live forever inside the server.

00:19:49.630 --> 00:19:53.430
But for me, the real thing
is a lot more dazzling.

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:58.800
The real blue skies, the real flowers,
the waves and the wind...

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:05.240
I wanted to touch all creation
in the world for real.

00:20:05.810 --> 00:20:08.510
So that, in the real world
that Yehl made for us...

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:14.540
I could pick a flower, like this.

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:24.590
That's why I think it's better to
have a limited life in the end.

00:20:25.360 --> 00:20:26.590
Yeah.

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:29.490
Your hair's gotten longer.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:31.900
Yeah.

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:35.840
With the fighting over, we were able
to increase the server's capacity.

00:20:35.840 --> 00:20:38.900
But the world still loops after a year.

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:42.240
Don't grow up too much, Kyo.

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:45.780
Just wait two years!

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:48.150
I promise,
I'll be there for graduation.

00:20:48.150 --> 00:20:49.620
Sure. I'll wait.

00:20:54.860 --> 00:20:58.800
Ah, there it is! I'm starving!

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:00.430
Let's go, Kaminagi!

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:01.730
Right!

00:22:43.700 --> 00:22:48.400
Hurry up and be born.
The world's waiting and it's full of light!
